From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] package/db: tag riscv64 wheels as manylinux_2_39_riscv64

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/voxel51/fiftyone/pull/8637]

With the previous patch alone, riscv64 wheels get a valid but generic
linux_riscv64 tag, which PyPI (and our own registry) rejects as not a
recognized platform tag.

Add an explicit riscv64 branch in finalize_options(), matching the
official manylinux riscv64 baseline (glibc 2.39), the same way the
other Linux architectures are handled.

Backported from the upstream PR linked above (not yet merged). As that
PR notes, MongoDB ships no riscv64 binary, so on this platform the
wheel builds and installs cleanly but without a bundled mongod -
_get_download() finds no riscv64 entry in LINUX_DOWNLOADS, returns
None, and write_wheelfile() leaves fiftyone/db/bin/ empty instead of
raising. Callers must point fiftyone at an external MongoDB via
database_uri, exactly as fiftyone's own docs already describe for any
platform lacking a bundled mongod.
---
 package/db/setup.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/package/db/setup.py b/package/db/setup.py
index 50092223882..d37d33ceea9 100644
--- a/package/db/setup.py
+++ b/package/db/setup.py
@@ -219,6 +219,8 @@ def finalize_options(self):
             self.plat_name = "manylinux1_i686"
         elif is_platform("Linux", "aarch64"):
             self.plat_name = "manylinux2014_aarch64"
+        elif is_platform("Linux", "riscv64"):
+            self.plat_name = "manylinux_2_39_riscv64"
         elif is_platform("Linux", "x86_64"):
             self.plat_name = "manylinux1_x86_64"
         elif is_platform("Darwin", "arm64"):
